We have three congruent isosceles triangles $DAO$, $AOB$ and $OBC$ with $AD=AO=OB=BC=10$ and $AB=DO=OC=12$. These triangles are arranged to form the trapezoid $ABCD$, as shown.

$\text{Draw a diagram.}$

[asy]
pair A, B, C, D, O, P;
A= (6, 8);
B=(18, 8);
C=(24, 0);
D=(0,0);
O=(12,0);
P=(12,8);
draw(A--B--C--D--A);
draw(A--O--B);
draw(O--P, dashed);
label("A", A, NW);
label("B", B, NE);
label("C", C, SE);
label("D", D, SW);
label("O", O, S);
label("P", P, N);
label("12", (D+O)/2, S);
label("12", (O+C)/2, S);
label("10", (A+D)/2, NW);
label("10", (B+C)/2, NE);
[/asy]

$\text{Point  X is the midpoint of  AD  and point } Y \text{ is the midpoint of } BC$

$X=(A+D)/2=(6+0)/2 \implies X: (3, 0)$

$Y=(B+C)/2=(18+24)/2 \implies Y: (21, 0)$

$\text{When  X  and  Y  are joined,  trapezoid  is divided into two smaller  trapezoids }$

$\text{The ratio of the area of  trapezoid }ABYX \text{ to the area of trapezoid }XYCD \text{ in simplified form is } 8:4$

$\implies \text{ p+q=8+4=12 }$

$\text{Area=?}$

$\text{($ \text{triangle  }$  OPB=($\frac{(x^2/2)+120+1}{2}$)} xmax(12,6))$}$
\begin{推导}OP&=sqrt(AO^2-AP^2)=sqrt(100-6^2)=8</推导>

由此，三角形$OPB$的面积等于$\frac{BO \times OP}{2} = \frac{12 \times 8}{2} \approx 48$.

所以，$trapezoid ABYX$的面积大约是$\frac{10 \times 8}{2} \approx 40$.

$trapezoid XYCD$的面积大约是$\frac{10 \times 8}{2} \approx 40$.

因此，$trapezoid ABYX$与$trapezoid XYCD$的面积比大约是$40:40=8:4$.

因此，$p+q=8+4=12$.
